.TH "VIDEOCOLORSPACE.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VideoColorSpace.toJSON \- VideoColorSpace: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]VideoColorSpace\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable plain
object representing the \f[CR]VideoColorSpace\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]VideoColorSpace\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
The serialized value can then be deserialized using the
\f[CR]VideoColorSpace()\f[R] constructor within the reviver of
\f[CR]JSON.parse()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]fullRange\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]matrix\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]primaries\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]transfer\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object containing
the \f[CR]VideoColorSpace\f[R] object\(cqs properties.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] colorSpace = \f[B]new\f[R] VideoColorSpace({
  primaries: \(dqbt709\(dq,
  transfer: \(dqbt709\(dq,
  matrix: \(dqbt709\(dq,
  fullRange: \f[B]true\f[R],
});

\f[B]const\f[R] json = colorSpace.toJSON();
console.log(json);
\f[I]// { fullRange: true, matrix: \(dqbt709\(dq, primaries: \(dqbt709\(dq, transfer: \(dqbt709\(dq }\f[R]
console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
The \f[CR]VideoColorSpace\f[R] object from the previous example is
serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the
\f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(colorSpace));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqfullRange\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R],
  \(dqmatrix\(dq: \(dqbt709\(dq,
  \(dqprimaries\(dq: \(dqbt709\(dq,
  \(dqtransfer\(dq: \(dqbt709\(dq
}
.EE
